## Decisions

### Production redeploys on commits that only touch TODO.md, and .gcloudignore can't stop that. May I add a file filter to the `build-main` Cloud Build trigger so these commits stop deploying, and if so, which filter?

**What I found.** Production is deployed by one Cloud Build trigger, `build-main` (project `heliosian`, region `us-west1`). It fires on every push to `main` through the GitHub connection. It clones the commit and runs `docker build`, `docker push`, `gcloud run deploy`. Nothing in the trigger filters by file, so `gcloud builds triggers describe build-main --region us-west1 --project heliosian` shows only `push: branch: ^main$`, with no `includedFiles` or `ignoredFiles`.

`.gcloudignore` doesn't affect this. It only controls what `gcloud builds submit` uploads from a local checkout, and a GitHub-triggered build never reads it. Adding entries there won't change anything. `.dockerignore` only trims the Docker build context. It doesn't decide whether a build runs either. The only thing that can skip a build is a file filter on the trigger itself.

**It's happening right now.** These are the builds currently queued:
| build | commit | files changed |
|---|---|---|
| fa70b1e7 QUEUED | a0e74ea9 Verify workflow instructions | AGENTS.md, TODO.md |
| 2f018280 QUEUED | f1f5fff2 Verify production | TODO.md |
| c6671bb8 QUEUED | b0625ff1 (newer than my checkout) | not checked |

Earlier, a76cca6e (TODO.md plus `tools/import/calendar.go`) built and deployed too. `tools/` isn't part of the server binary: the Dockerfile builds only the root package (`go build .` → `main.go` + `internal/`), and no server code imports `tools/`.

**What the image is built from:** `main.go`, `go.mod`, `go.sum`, `internal/**` (the binary; `internal/ask/prompt.md` is embedded, which is covered), `web/**` (copied in), and `Dockerfile` / `.dockerignore`.

**The change, whichever filter you pick:** export the trigger, add the filter, then import it back: `gcloud builds triggers export build-main --region us-west1 --project heliosian --destination <scratch>` → edit → `gcloud builds triggers import --region us-west1 --project heliosian --source <scratch>`. This writes to production's trigger, so I need your yes first. I'd also add one sentence to `docs/deploy.md` saying that pushes touching nothing in the image don't deploy, and pointing at `triggers describe` for the list.

Here's how each filter would treat the last six commits:
| commit | files | no filter (today) | allowlist | denylist |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| f1f5fff2 Verify production | TODO.md | deploys | skipped | skipped |
| a0e74ea9 Verify workflow instructions | AGENTS.md, TODO.md | deploys | skipped | skipped |
| 20d0f175 My Email Lists' intro… | TODO.md, docs/loop/loop.md, internal/app/about.go, internal/app/about_test.go, web/loop/pages/groups.js | deploys | deploys | deploys |
| a76cca6e Name the year calendar document… | TODO.md, tools/import/calendar.go | deploys | skipped | skipped |
| 139b54fd New Email List button… | TODO.md, docs/loop/loop.md, web/common/rail.js, web/loop/chrome.js, web/loop/pages/groups.js | deploys | deploys | deploys |
| 5c70290b Verify deploys after they come up | AGENTS.md | deploys | skipped | skipped |

- (*) Allowlist: build only when image inputs change
  Adds `includedFiles: [main.go, go.mod, go.sum, Dockerfile, .dockerignore, "internal/**", "web/**"]`. It's one list that names exactly what the Dockerfile uses. A new top-level doc or folder never deploys without anyone having to remember to add it. The risk: a new top-level code directory outside `internal/` would need adding to the list, or its changes wouldn't deploy. Nothing like that exists today.
- ( ) Denylist: skip when only non-image files change
  Adds `ignoredFiles: [TODO.md, README.md, AGENTS.md, LICENSE.md, .gitignore, .gcloudignore, "docs/**", "tools/**", "sampledata/**", "asset-sources/**", ".claude/**"]`. It gives the same results on these six commits. Any new path deploys by default, so it fails safe toward deploying, but every new non-code file or folder needs adding to the list or it deploys again.
- ( ) Leave the trigger alone
  Nothing changes. TODO.md, AGENTS.md and docs pushes keep redeploying production.

ian@fc.run chose: Allowlist: build only when image inputs change
